  "summary": "METR reports that leading AI models like Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra are improving rapidly at research tasks but getting harder to measure. Current data can't rule out a dangerous acceleration in AI development, the organization warns, though it also says common tests may overestimate what the models can actually do. The article AI is getting better faster than experts can reliably test whether new systems are safe, METR warns appeared first on The Decoder .",
